{
  "schema": "malspark-host-benign-locations/v1",
  "version": "2.0",
  "source": "Windows itself, as Microsoft documents it: the Known Folders and CSIDL references, the folders Windows Setup creates under %SystemRoot%, the files Windows ships there, the services and named pipes Windows' own components install and open, the streams Windows writes, the registry keys and values every installation holds, the object manager's namespaces, and the Task Scheduler task-definition schema. Nothing here is about one sample, family or run; each list states the criterion that admits an entry. Written for this project, not copied from a third-party table.",
  "about": "Host values every Windows system holds or every program may use, which a value the analysis states is refused as: an indicator on one matches every host. Compared case-insensitively, a path with '/' read as '\\\\' and each component with trailing dots and spaces trimmed (Windows ignores them). A component is a known folder when it is in 'known_folders', 'environment_folders' or 'system_folders', begins with a 'known_folder_prefixes' entry, is a drive, is the profile name after 'Users', or is the 8.3 short name Windows generates for a known folder (its first six letters without spaces, a tilde and a digit). 'generic_names' are not refused: such a value is exported with a note that it may match ordinary software, and never becomes a matcher on its own.",
